## 4. `include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp` — Split Model Shard Resolution

**Responsibilities:** Resolves the shard paths of a split GGUF model from any shard's filename, validates that all shards exist, and returns them in order.

**Proposed change:** Add a `gguf_split_paths_optional()` variant that returns an empty vector instead of throwing when a shard is missing, for use in diagnostic tools that want to report partial availability without exception handling.

```diff
--- a/include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp
@@ -40,6 +40,22 @@
     return out;
 }

+/// Like gguf_split_paths but returns only the shards that exist (empty if none).
+inline std::vector<std::string> gguf_split_paths_optional(const std::string& any) {
+    static const char tag[] = "-of-";
+    const size_t at = any.rfind(tag);
+    if (at == std::string::npos || at < 6 || any[at - 6] != '-' || any.size() != at + 4 + 5 + 5 ||
+        any.compare(at + 9, 5, ".gguf") != 0)
+        return {any};
+    int no = 0, n = 0;
+    for (size_t i = 0; i < 5; ++i) {
+        const char a = any[at - 5 + i], b = any[at + 4 + i];
+        if (a < '0' || a > '9' || b < '0' || b > '9') return {any};
+        no = no * 10 + (a - '0');
+        n = n * 10 + (b - '0');
+    }
+    if (n < 1 || no < 1 || no > n) return {any};
+    std::vector<std::string> out;
+    for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {
+        char num[8];
+        std::snprintf(num, sizeof num, "%05d", i);
+        std::string p = any;
+        p.replace(at - 5, 5, num);
+        if (std::ifstream(p, std::ios::binary)) out.push_back(std::move(p));
+    }
+    return out;
+}
+
 }  // namespace strata
```

**Verification cases:**
1. Point at a 4-shard model where shard 3 is deleted; confirm `gguf_split_paths` throws naming shard 3, while `gguf_split_paths_optional` returns 3 paths (1, 2, 4).
2. Point at a non-split file; both functions return a single-element vector with the original path.

